  SCENARIO
  =================
  Mr TAN AH BENG (70 y/o male, NRIC S5512345A) — the same cardiology patient
  used in the medication samples (AF + HTN). During allergy reconciliation at
  his 2026-05-12 visit with Dr Ruth Kam (MCR 04173D), a long-standing ASPIRIN
  allergy is documented: he developed widespread urticaria (hives) on a prior
  aspirin exposure in 2015. Clinically important here — aspirin is core
  antiplatelet therapy, so the alert must flag "avoid same drug AND same class".

  This is a DRUG ALLERGY (an immune-mediated allergic reaction), so:
    verificationStatus.code = "Y"  (CMIS_DRUG_ALLERGY_INDICATOR: Yes, it is an allergy)
    reportingFlag.code       = "A"  (new report)
    drugType                 = "S"  (suspected/causative drug)
    drugProbability.code     = "1"  (Definite)

  ANNOTATION FORMAT
  =================
  Each element comment carries three pieces:
    [M | O | C]            Significance:  M = Mandatory
                                          O = Optional
                                          C = Conditional Mandatory
    Cardinality            e.g. "1", "0..1", "0..*"
    Data type / length     e.g. "String(50)", "DateTime", "Grouping"
  Plus inline justification for the populated value.

  NO-EMPTY-TAGS RULE
  =================
  Per Synapxe Guide v0.42 / Readme tab: omit empty elements entirely. Do NOT
  emit <tag/>, </tag> or <tag>NA</tag> for unmapped fields. Optional fields not
  in use are shown as commented-out reminders for the developer.

  CODESET NOTES (all REAL values from CodeSetInventory v2.29, 24 Dec 2025)
  =================
    reportingFlag        CMIS_REPORTING_FLAG_(NEHR)          A  = Add a new report
    verificationStatus   CMIS_DRUG_ALLERGY_INDICATOR_(NEHR)  Y  = Yes (allergy)
    informationSource    CMIS_INFORMATION_SOURCE_(NEHR)      01 = Reporter observation
    profession           CMIS_REPORTER_PROFESSION_(NEHR)     2  = Doctor
    ADRAlertIndicator    CMIS_ADR_ALERT_INDICATOR_(NEHR)     1  = Avoid same drug + same class
    severity (serious?)  CMIS_REACTION_SEVERITY_(NEHR)       N  = No (not life-threatening)
    ADROutcome           CMIS_ADR_OUTCOME_(NEHR)             1  = Recovered
    substance (allergen) CMIS_DRUG_(NEHR)                    A01060 = Aspirin
    productName (brand)  CMIS_BRAND_(NEHR)                   B00379 = Aspirin - Beacons
    exposureRoute        CMIS_ADMINISTRATION_ROUTE_(NEHR)    038 = Oral
    drugProbability      CMIS_DRUG_PROBABILITY_(NEHR)        1  = Definite
  IMPORTANT: CMIS code-sets carry Start_Date / End_Date. Validate the codes
  above are live (see "Expired Codes" tab of the spec) before SIT submission.
================================================================================
-->

